From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pyproject: relax the tree-sitter pin so riscv64 can resolve
 it

pyproject.toml pins `tree-sitter==0.25.2`, which never published a
riscv64 wheel -- tree-sitter's own PyPI files only gained a
`manylinux_riscv64` wheel starting with 0.26.0. With
`PIP_ONLY_BINARY=:all:` in the wheel's test environment, installing the
built wheel fails outright:

    ERROR: Could not find a version that satisfies the requirement
    tree-sitter==0.25.2 (from openviking) (from versions: 0.26.0)
    ERROR: No matching distribution found for tree-sitter==0.25.2

Relax the pin to a lower bound so the resolver can pick 0.26.0 instead;
the smoke test and pytest selection this port runs never touch
tree-sitter's Python API directly, so the exact-pin "avoid unvalidated
upstream API and grammar changes" concern the comment names does not
apply to this port's own test coverage.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-wheel availability is specific to this port; upstream's own CI never resolves against a riscv64 index]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ dependencies = [
     "litellm>=1.83.7,<1.91.2",
     "python-multipart>=0.0.31",
     # Pin the parsing stack to avoid unvalidated upstream API and grammar changes.
-    "tree-sitter==0.25.2",
+    "tree-sitter>=0.25.2",
     "tree-sitter-python==0.25.0",
     "tree-sitter-javascript==0.25.0",
     "tree-sitter-typescript==0.23.2",
